mods.description:
Bids and sales at the auction house by command, and your listings in the log (the auction helper add-ons).

//ahbuy <item> <price> [stack]
//ahsell <item> <price> [stack]
//ahlist

Saves your automaton's head, frame and attachments as named sets and puts a set on with one command (the automaton set add-ons).

//automaton save <name>
//automaton <name>
//automaton list
//automaton delete <name>

Moves items between your bags by command: fetch and stow by name, gather the gear your Gearshift file names, tidy the rest away (the organizer and porter add-ons).

//stow get <item> [count | all]
//stow put <item> [to <bag>] [all]
//stow gear
//stow tidy

Saves your set blue magic as named sets and puts a set back with one command; a codex of every blue spell and what teaches it; a call when a monster readies a move that teaches one you lack (the blue magic add-ons).

//blu save <name>
//blu <name>
//blu list
//blu delete <name>
//blu codex

Works out sums in the chat line or a small window: gil, stacks, prices (the calculator add-ons).

//calc <sum>
//calc (opens the window)

A window of its own for a chat channel (tells, party, linkshells, say, shout, yell, unity) with a line to answer in, and a search over the session's lines (the chat window add-ons).

//chatwin <tell | party | ls | ls2 | say | shout | yell | unity>
//chatfind <words>

What is left to do: the spells a job has yet to learn and every area's quests, done, under way or not started (the checklist add-ons).

//left
//left spells [job]
//left quests

A window for the content you are in: Dynamis, Abyssea, Salvage, Nyzul Isle, Omen, Delve, Odyssey, Sortie or a reive, with the time left and what the content's messages tell; pop lists for the Empyrean and Zeni NMs (the content tracker add-ons).

//pops [NM]
//znm

Your own countdowns as rows in the Timers windows, with a line when each is up (the timer add-ons).

//timer <time> <name> (90, 5m, 1h30m or 2:30)
//timer cancel <name>
//timer clear

Renames characters and monsters on your screen, hides your own name plate, and sets your size (the renamer and name plate add-ons). Only you see it.

//rename <name> as <new name>
//rename <name> (undo)
//renames

Runs your command lines when things happen: a zone, a job, an effect gained or lost, HP or MP low, a word in chat, a new day or weather (the auto-exec add-ons).

//rules (lists them)
//rules reload

Swaps gear around your actions from GearSwap job files and LuAshitacast and Ashitacast XML profiles, unchanged (the gear-swap add-ons).

//gs: GearSwap's own commands
//lac: LuAshitacast's own commands
//ac: Ashitacast's own commands
//spellcast: Spellcast's own commands
//gearshift shows the loaded file
//gearshift reload reads it again

Hotbars of multi-line macros with their actions' icons and recasts, loaded by main job and sub job.

//hb (opens the manager)
//hb show
//hb hide
//hb run <bar> <slot>
//hb reload
//hb wipestock
//hb restorestock

Bag space, gil and the items and key items you choose, in a window on a screen edge (the inventory and gil tracker add-ons).

//bags add <item>
//bags addkey <key item>
//bags remove <name>
//bags list

Binds keys to command lines and makes short aliases for long commands, kept per character (the bind and alias add-ons).

//bind <key> <line>
//unbind <key>
//binds
//alias <name> <line>
//unalias <name>
//aliases

Numbers the web links in chat so you can open or copy them (the chat link add-ons).

//links (lists them)
//links <number> opens one

Spells, abilities and mounts you never use left out of the game's lists, kept per character (the list trimming add-ons).

//trim <spell, ability or mount>
//trim list
//trim clear

Changes how characters look on your screen only: your race, face and gear, a target's look copied, one race for everyone else (the dress-up add-ons).

//look race <race>
//look face <1a..8b>
//look <slot> <item | none | own>
//look copy [name]
//look others <race | own>
//look reset

Lots, passes and drops treasure by your lists (the treasury and loot add-ons).

//loot [lot | pass | drop] [add | remove] <item>
//loot list

Turns the macro palette to the book and set you keep for each job when the job changes (the macro changer add-ons).

//macros save [sub]
//macros forget [sub]
//macros list

Notes pinned to places on a zone's map, your party and the monsters you track, marked on the Map Overlay (the map marker add-ons).

//mapnote add <text>
//mapnote del <n>
//mapnote list
//mapnote track <name>
//mapnote untrack <name>

A bar across the top of the screen with the zone, the time and weather, and your target: its /check result and the notes you keep on it (the info bar add-ons).

//mobnote (shows the target's note)
//mobnote <text>
//mobnote clear

Calls a random mount of yours, or one by part of its name (the mount roulette add-ons).

//ride (a random mount)
//ride <part of a name>
//ride list

Commands, targets and status removal sent to your other game windows on this machine, focus switching, and tells relayed between them (the multibox add-ons).

//send <name | all | others> <command>
//sendtarget [name]
//focus <name>
//stna [name]

Plays any of the game's tracks, keeps the zone's music in battle or silences it while mounted (the music add-ons).

//music <track number>
//music off

Walks an NPC's menus by command, keeps such errands by name, and changes jobs at a moogle by command (the NPC shop and job change add-ons).

//npc <name>: <option> > <option> > ...
//errand <name>
//errand save <name> <npc>: <option> > ...
//errand list
//errand delete <name>
//job <main>[/<sub>]

Saves the Records of Eminence objectives you have set as named sets and puts a set back with one command (the objective set add-ons).

//roeset save <name>
//roeset <name>
//roeset list
//roeset delete <name>
//roeshow

Screenshots filed in folders by character and zone, and video recording by command (the screenshot organizer and capture add-ons).

//shot
//record
//record stop

Puts your own notes on the screen by command, where you drag them (the text add-ons).

//note <name> <text>
//note <name> (removes it)
//notes

Sells items by name to the open shop and hands items to your target NPC by command (the sell and trade add-ons).

//sell <item> [all]
//trade <item> [count], <item> [count]...

Targets by name or id, turns you toward or away from your target, and can check each monster you target (the targeting add-ons).

//tgt <name or server id>
//face
//face away

Keeps the tells that come while you are away, answers the last tell with //r, and can send an away reply (the answering machine add-ons).

//r <message>
//tells

Tracks a monster or NPC by name with Wide Scan, and lists who in the zone matches a name (the wide scan add-ons).

//track <name>
//track stop
//seek <name>

Saves the trusts you call as named lineups and calls a lineup with one command (the trust set add-ons).

//trusts <lineup>
//trusts save <lineup> [trust, trust...]
//trusts list
//trusts delete <lineup>

Uses every copy of an item one after another, such as a stack of pouches or bags (the pouch add-ons).

//useall <item>
//useall stop

Answers the Home Point, Survival Guide and Waypoint menus by name, and warps home with the Warp spell or a warp item (the warp add-ons).

//warp [hp | sg | wp] <zone> [number or place]
//warp home
//warp dim <holla | dem | mea>

Looks up an item, a spell, your target or any words on the wiki or the auction site, in your browser (the lookup add-ons).

//wiki [words]
//ah [words] (no words: the item pointed at or your target)

Puts the game window back where and how big you keep it for each character, and can keep it on top (the window position add-ons).

//winpos save
//winpos forget
